  "notes": "A compound verb from {植|う}える (to plant) + {替|か}える (to replace/change). Primarily a gardening term.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {鉢|はち}に{植|う}え{替|か}える: to repot\n- {庭|にわ}に{植|う}え{替|か}える: to transplant into the garden\n- {苗|なえ}を{植|う}え{替|か}える: to transplant seedlings\n- {植|う}え{替|か}えの{時期|じき}: repotting season\n\nUSAGE:\nThe noun form is {植|う}え{替|か}え. Spring is the most common season for repotting in Japan. Plants need repotting when {根|ね}が{詰|つ}まる (roots become crowded) or {土|つち}が{古|ふる}くなる (soil becomes old).",
